  {
   "id": 1,
   "ref": "547–552",
   "en": "'No — die, as [you deserve|4,5], and put an end to your grief with the sword. You, sister, gave way to my tears, and it was you who first loaded me down, mad as I already was, with all this suffering, and threw me to my enemy. [I was not allowed|23,24] to live out my life, [innocent|27,28], untouched by marriage, the way a wild creature does, [free of|34,35] troubles like these. The vow I made to Sychaeus's ashes — I have not kept it.'",
   "en_marked": "'[No|1] — [die|2], [as|3] [you deserve|4,5], [and|6] [put an end to|7] your [grief|8] with [the sword|6]. [You|9], [sister|17], [gave way|11] to [my|12] [tears|10], and it was [you|13] who [first|14] [loaded|19] me down, [mad as I|15] {already|Added. furentem means raving; already shows Dido was mad with love before Anna encouraged her.} [was|15], with {all|Added for emphasis; his malis means simply with these troubles.} [this|16] [suffering|18], [and|20] [threw|21] me to my [enemy|22]. [I was not allowed|23,24] [to live out|30] my [life|29], [innocent|27,28], [untouched|26] by [marriage|25], [the way|31] a [wild creature|32] does, [free of|34,35] [troubles|36] [like these|33]. The [vow|39] I [made|41] to [Sychaeus's|42] [ashes|40] — I [have not|37] [kept|38] it.'",
